For the state prediction we start by calculating the marginal state distribution (MSD) matrix. MSD is an N × K matrix that for each cell is marginalizing the transition probability over all possible current states by traversing from root to leaf cells:4\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$M{SD}\left(n,k\right)=P\left({z}_{n}=k\right)=\mathop{\sum}\limits _{i}P\left({z}_{n}=k{{{{{\rm{|}}}}}}{z}_{n-1}=i\right)\times P\left({z}_{n-1}=i\right)$$\end{document}MSDn,k=Pzn=k=∑iPzn=k∣zn−1=i×Pzn−1=i

During upward recursion, the flow of upward probabilities is calculated from leaf cells to the root cells generation by generation. First, for leaf cells, the probabilities (β) are calculated by:5\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${\beta }_{n}\left(k\right)=P\left({z}_{n}=k{{{{{\rm{|}}}}}}{X}_{n}={x}_{n}\right)=\frac{{EL}\left(n,k\right)\times {MSD}\left(n,k\right)}{N{F}_{l}\left(n\right)}$$\end{document}βnk=Pzn=k∣Xn=xn=ELn,k×MSDn,kNFlnin which Xn is the leaf cell’s observation, and NF (Normalizing Factor) is an N × 1 matrix that is the marginal observation distribution. Since \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${\sum }_{k}{\beta }_{n}(k)=1$$\end{document}∑kβn(k)=1, we find the NF for leaf cells using:6\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$N{F}_{l}(n)=\mathop{\sum}\limits _{k}EL(n,k)\times MSD(n,k)=P({X}_{n}={x}_{n})$$\end{document}NFl(n)=∑kEL(n,k)×MSD(n,k)=P(Xn=xn)

For non-leaf cells the values are given by:7\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${\beta }_{n}(k)=P({z}_{n}=k|{\bar{X}}_{n}={\bar{x}}_{n})=\frac{EL(n,k)\times MSD(n,k)\times {\prod }_{v\in c(n)}{\beta }_{n,v}(k)}{N{F}_{nl}(n)}$$\end{document}βn(k)=P(zn=k∣X¯n=x¯n)=EL(n,k)×MSD(n,k)×∏v∈c(n)βn,v(k)NFnl(n)where we calculate the non-leaf NF using:8\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$N{F}_{nl}(n)=\mathop{\sum}\limits _{k}\left[EL(n,k)\times MSD(n,k)\mathop{\prod}\limits_{v\in c(n)}{\beta }_{n,v}(k)\right]$$\end{document}NFnl(n)=∑kEL(n,k)×MSD(n,k)∏v∈c(n)βn,v(k)and linking β between parent-daughter cells is given by:9\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${\beta }_{p(n),n}(k)=P({\bar{X}}_{n}={\bar{x}}_{n}|{z}_{p(n)}=k)=\mathop{\sum}\limits _{j}\frac{{\beta }_{n}(j)\times {T}_{k,j}}{MSD(n,j)}$$\end{document}βp(n),n(k)=P(X¯n=x¯n∣zp(n)=k)=∑jβn(j)×Tk,jMSD(n,j)

By recursing from leaf to root cells, the β and NF matrices are calculated as upward recursion. The NF matrix gives a convenient expression for the observation log-likelihoods. For each root cell we have:10\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$\begin{array}{cc}P(\bar{X}=\bar{x})=\mathop{\prod}\limits _{n}\frac{P({\bar{X}}_{n}={\bar{x}}_{n})}{{\prod }_{v\in c(n)}P({\bar{X}}_{v}={\bar{x}}_{v})}=\mathop{\sum}\limits_{n}NF(n) & n\in \{1,\ldots ,N\}\end{array}$$\end{document}P(X¯=x¯)=∏nP(X¯n=x¯n)∏v∈c(n)P(X¯v=x¯v)=∑nNF(n)n∈{1,…,N}

The overall model log-likelihood is given by the sum over root cells:11\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$logP(\bar{X}=\bar{x})=\mathop{\sum}\limits_{n}\log NF(n)$$\end{document}logP(X¯=x¯)=∑nlogNF(n)

For computing downward recursion, we need the following definition for each root cells:12\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
