				\begin{document}$${\gamma }_{1}(k)=P({z}_{1}=k|{\bar{X}}_{1}={\bar{x}}_{1})={\beta }_{1}(k)$$\end{document}γ1(k)=P(z1=k∣X¯1=x¯1)=β1(k)

The other cells follow in an N × K matrix by writing the conditional probabilities as the summation over the joint probabilities of parent-daughter cell:13\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${\gamma }_{n}(k)=P({z}_{n}=k|{\bar{X}}_{1}={\bar{x}}_{1})=\frac{{\beta }_{n}(k)}{MSD(n,k)}\mathop{\sum}\limits_{i}\frac{{T}_{i,k}{\gamma }_{p(n)}(i)}{{\beta }_{p(n),n}(i)}$$\end{document}γn(k)=P(zn=k∣X¯1=x¯1)=βn(k)MSD(n,k)∑iTi,kγp(n)(i)βp(n),n(i)

The algorithm follows an upward recursion from leaf to root cells. We define δ, an N × K matrix:14\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
