				\begin{document}$$P\left({z}_{n}=k,{z}_{n+1}=l{{{{{\rm{|}}}}}}{X}_{n}\right)$$\end{document}Pzn=k,zn+1=l∣Xn. The expectation step is calculated by the upward and downward recursion algorithms described above. In the maximization step, described above, the distribution parameters of each state, the initial (π) probabilities, and the transition probability (T) matrices are estimated, given the state assignments of each cell.

